{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795171279,"nonce":"TAPN38Tszziistnvjd9y4ajHwro=","message":"Studied local Blinc 96cbd5d0200b54ea307910b14918a73971cbe637 and blinc_abi bda6be7dd5db6fb1cab694a78056dfcc0453d811. Also checked upstream main's blinc_text Cargo.toml and shaper.rs. Current shaping uses rustybuzz 0.20. The user clarified that the intended migration is HarfRust, not native HarfBuzz. Blinc already tracks that migration in its own open issue 7f644d9947e67521d5dae7778c42bb091aa8855e3e5c384388f0cb0982eec05a. No migration was implemented during this research.\n\nRecommendation proposed to the user, not yet an accepted implementation decision: depend on the shared blinc_text engine behind an hxn-generated API rather than clone it or link the entire blinc_abi. Keep engine fixes and the HarfRust migration upstream in Blinc. Reuse relevant regression fixtures and add installed Haxe API checks. blinc_text currently reaches blinc_core only for Linux system-font family constants; evaluate isolating that dependency. blinc_abi remains a reference for owned fonts and incremental atlas delivery, without importing its CSS/layout/scene/runtime boundary.\n\nUseful source paths and lessons:\n- Blinc crates/blinc_text/src/font.rs and registry.rs: owned/shared Arc font bytes, native memory maps, explicit collection face indexes, lazy discovery, style-aware lookup, immutable registered faces and registry generations. Shaping and rasterization must use the same variation settings and fallback advances.\n- blinc_abi src/font.rs: decode owned TTF/OTF/WOFF2 data, private immutable per-resource/weight aliases, unregister aliases on drop while retained faces keep their bytes alive. Its README records a WOFF2 transformed-hmtx limitation. URL/asset loading belongs to the consumer, which maps to hxn-file/hxn-assets for hxn-text.\n- Blinc shaper.rs caches parsed faces and shape plans by face identity/variation and segment properties. HarfRust uses read-fonts-based parsing and different shaper/instance APIs, so migration is not a dependency rename. Its upstream README states that glyph positions are in font units and callers scale them.\n- rasterizer.rs uses swash for alpha/color glyphs, with variation weight and subpixel offset. CFF needs its specific hinting treatment. colr/mod.rs renders COLRv1 through ttf-parser/tiny-skia and normalizes straight RGBA. iOS apple.rs resolves fonts and renders Apple-specific color/hvgl outlines through CoreText/CoreGraphics.\n- atlas.rs provides separate alpha and RGBA atlases, dirty rectangles, shelf packing, bounded growth and reclamation. blinc_abi src/text.rs exposes packed glyph instances and revisioned dirty-rectangle history (full upload when a consumer is too old); clear generations invalidate retained rectangles. Pixel atlas coordinates survive growth better than baked normalized UVs. Raster size follows display/transform scale with bounded buckets and optional horizontal subpixel phases.\n\nGaps to retain in hxn-text acceptance: the current layout shapes a whole string with guessed segment properties and does not use the declared unicode-bidi dependency for explicit bidi/script segmentation. Fallback includes per-character substitution and dedicated emoji/CJK handling; this is not evidence of full multi-script shaping correctness. No text SDF/MSDF generator was found in the studied path. Blinc's own open issues 566784ba69d16a2ab8e6800d7327b87da67f7482158c760db255f9b00bf13d23 (half-pixel atlas key collisions) and 36eae86550152cc49c03cce8ecc3d20e9442f7f9dd5089dcd94a7a1753f699e5 (iOS simulator font discovery) document relevant gaps. Browser initialization explicitly requires bundled/fetched font bytes and refreshing generic-font resolution after registration. Add mixed RTL/LTR, Arabic/Indic joining, fallback clusters, variable axes, invalid fonts, hot replacement, atlas growth/clear, mobile/system-font and browser asset tests through the hxn API. tests/shape_plans.rs exists but is not included in tests/main.rs while autotests=false, so it was not part of the normal test run.\n\nValidation on this macOS host under timeouts: cargo test --locked -p blinc_text --lib --test integration passed (59 unit + 29 integration tests). blinc_abi cargo test --locked --no-default-features --features scene font::tests passed (2 tests), including invalid data, TTF/WOFF2 equivalence and owned alias lifetime. The ABI lock uses older Blinc 2c1745b7250cca69dd2e736c6416d992fbaf3f39, not the local Blinc head. These runs do not establish browser, Android, iOS or Windows correctness. Source worktrees were unchanged; Blinc's pre-existing untracked HANDOFF.md was untouched. No commits, pushes or git-bug push.","files":null}]}